            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, the central legal question is whether an equitable remedy, such as an injunction, is available under ERISA when the federal statute provides no explicit legal remedy."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d58406068da091f0795a4fe25a49fc77045ad8be6f794b1c2983fb9ceb8440b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d58406068da-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, a related question is whether the phrase \u201cenjoin any act\u201d in \u00a7502(a)(3)(A) includes a failure to act."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Questioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d58406068da091f0795a4fe25a49fc77045ad8be6f794b1c2983fb9ceb8440b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d58406068da-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 35,
              "start": 35
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Questioner, another issue raised is the oddity that a body of federal common law would be applied only in state courts."
      }
    ],
