            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked whether, because the federal statute provides no legal remedy, an equitable remedy is available under ERISA."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d58406068da091f0795a4fe25a49fc77045ad8be6f794b1c2983fb9ceb8440b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d58406068da-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 26,
              "start": 26
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, he further queried whether the phrase \u201cenjoin any act\u201d includes a failure to act."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Questioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d58406068da091f0795a4fe25a49fc77045ad8be6f794b1c2983fb9ceb8440b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d58406068da-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 35,
              "start": 35
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Questioner, a questioner noted the oddity that a body of federal common law would be applied only in state courts."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Taranto",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d58406068da091f0795a4fe25a49fc77045ad8be6f794b1c2983fb9ceb8440b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d58406068da-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Mr. Taranto argued that state tort law creates a negligence claim and that subrogation should follow the terms of the ERISA plan, allowing the plan to step into the beneficiary\u2019s shoes."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Taranto",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d58406068da091f0795a4fe25a49fc77045ad8be6f794b1c2983fb9ceb8440b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d58406068da-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Taranto, he contended that the preemption argument against the subrogation suit is weak and does not require a strong response."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Taranto",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d58406068da091f0795a4fe25a49fc77045ad8be6f794b1c2983fb9ceb8440b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d58406068da-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Taranto, he referenced legislative history indicating that earlier drafts of the provision allowed broader legal or equitable relief, which was later narrowed."
      }
    ],
