  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners (Great-West Life & Annuity Insurance Company)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d58406068da091f0795a4fe25a49fc77045ad8be6f794b1c2983fb9ceb8440b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d58406068da-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners (Great-West Life & Annuity Insurance Company), great\u2011West Life & Annuity Insurance Company (the petitioners) seek injunctive and declaratory relief to enforce a reimbursement clause in the employee benefit plan."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners (Great-West Life & Annuity Insurance Company)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d58406068da091f0795a4fe25a49fc77045ad8be6f794b1c2983fb9ceb8440b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d58406068da-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners (Great-West Life & Annuity Insurance Company), the petitioners argue that ERISA \u00a7502(a)(3)(A) authorizes a civil action to enjoin any act that violates the terms of the plan, supporting their request for an injunction against the respondents."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners (Great-West Life & Annuity Insurance Company)",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d58406068da091f0795a4fe25a49fc77045ad8be6f794b1c2983fb9ceb8440b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d58406068da-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 10,
              "start": 10
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners (Great-West Life & Annuity Insurance Company), section\u202f404(a) of ERISA obligates fiduciaries to enforce the terms of the plan, reinforcing the petitioners\u2019 claim."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "United States",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "1d58406068da091f0795a4fe25a49fc77045ad8be6f794b1c2983fb9ceb8440b",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-1d58406068da-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to United States, an amicus curiae brief filed on behalf of the United States supports the petitioners\u2019 position that the plan\u2019s enforcement mechanism is the only way to protect its terms."
      }
    ],
